004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:69cf606aa9b50eb6068cac867de9d6732f17c5bfc131d7d9b702124495d03d19", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:bd4fcb3cf8c389b31bb621a0261a5f77bd4143d3cd96e9046ab7733b7d2598d2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d5272c3dd5fcfa4085ac6698dc324e7169bdc1f40e6072c4c87c9934301f3733", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category. The construction of\nLemma <REF_0001>\npart (2) gives a functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>the 2-category of categories<MATHSEG_0002>fibred in setoids over <MATHSEG_0003>the category of categories<MATHSEG_0004>fibred in sets over <MATHSEG_0005>\n(see\nDefinition <REF_0002>).\nThis functor is an equivalence in the following sense:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> for any two 1-morphisms <MATH_0002>\nwith <MATH_0003> there exists a unique 2-isomorphism <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0004> for any morphism <MATH_0005>\nthere exists a 1-morphism <MATH_0006>\nwith <MATH_0007>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> any category fibred in sets <MATH_0008> is equal to <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nIn particular, defining <MATH_0010> by the\nrule <MATH_0011>, we have\n<MATHSEG_0006>-isomorphism<MATHSEG_0007>\nMore precisely, given any map <MATH_0012> there exists a\n<MATH_0013>-morphism <MATH_0014> which induces\n<MATH_0015> on isomorphism classes of objects and\nwhich is unique up to unique <MATH_0016>-isomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0007>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:124391ec0c471f357406d7a40c4d06402e1adf1010dcfafdad2e33829b900b84", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:04SC:lemma/0001"}}}], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:52dcf2584070b27c657ea972772b6b04258bf5c5e9660e2198a6807d66946759", "path": "translation-data/source-adoption-inputs/algebraic94-gpt61sol-p013-20261114-t01a1da14.json"}